# Spec: [Feature] (Jira PROJ-123)

> Produced by `/spec` (`spec-driven-development`). Human-approved before `/plan`. Keep living — update on scope/decision change. Delete or archive after merge if repo doesn't keep specs long-term.

## Objective
[What + why. Users, user stories, success metrics.]

## Tech Stack
- Backend: FastAPI 0.1xx, Python 3.12, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2.x/Alembic, pytest
- Frontend: React 18, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, vitest, playwright
- Local: `docker compose up --build`

## Commands
```
Dev: docker compose up --build
Backend test: pytest -q | lint: ruff check . | types: mypy backend/
Frontend dev: cd frontend && npm run dev | test: npm run test | lint: npm run lint | types: npx tsc --noEmit | e2e: npm run test:e2e
```

## Project Structure
```
backend/        → FastAPI app (routers/, services/, models/, schemas/)
frontend/       → React (components/ui shadcn, hooks/, lib/, app/ or src/)
docs/specs/     → This spec + capability maps
tasks/          → plan + todo for this Jira key
tests/e2e       → playwright specs
```

