[Framework, locations, pyramid split, coverage bar ≥80% touched, which levels for which concerns.]

## Boundaries
- Always: [tests before commit, validate inputs, link Jira+spec in MR]
- Ask first: [migrations, new deps, CI changes, public API changes]
- Never: [secrets, vendor/build output, force-push, untested legacy refactor]

## Threat model (REQUIRED for auth / personal data / payments / public API changes — else N/A with reason)
- Assets: [what must not leak/break]
- Trust boundaries: [where untrusted input crosses — routes, webhooks, file uploads]
- Mitigations: [authZ checks, validation, rate limits, audit logging per boundary]

## Success Criteria
- [ ] AC-1: Testable condition 1 (e.g. POST /items 201 + persisted, p95 < 300ms)
- [ ] AC-2: Testable condition 2 (e.g. empty-state UI keyboard-navigable, axe clean)

## Acceptance → Test map (TDD anchor — every AC gets ≥1 failing test BEFORE code)
| AC | Test file(s) | Level |
|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | `backend/tests/test_<area>.py::test_<case>` | unit / integration |
| AC-2 | `frontend/src/.../*.test.tsx` + `e2e/<flow>.spec.ts` | unit / e2e |
